{
  // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // SCOPE OF THE TYPE CHECK — READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING COVERAGE.
  //
  // `npm run typecheck` (astro check) reports 0 errors. That does NOT mean the
  // codebase type-checks. `checkJs` is FALSE, so:
  //
  //   CHECKED      src/loaders/skills.ts       (the only .ts file here)
  //                src/**/*.astro              (component script blocks)
  //
  //   NOT CHECKED — type errors in these are invisible to `astro check`:
  //                src/loaders/enumerate.mjs
  //                src/loaders/links.mjs
  //                src/loaders/markdown.mjs
  //                src/loaders/frontmatter.mjs
  //                src/loaders/site-pages.mjs
  //                src/sidebar.mjs
  //                src/site.config.mjs
  //                scripts/check-live-links.mjs
  //                scripts/prepare-assets.mjs
  //                tests/*.mjs
  //
  // That is most of the loader. Verified, not assumed: a `@type {number}`
  // annotation on a string constant, planted in enumerate.mjs and again in
  // sidebar.mjs, leaves `astro check` reporting 0 errors — while the same
  // class of error in skills.ts reports 1.
  //
  // CONSEQUENCE THAT BITES: the JSDoc `@typedef` blocks in enumerate.mjs and
  // frontmatter.mjs are INERT. They are accurate documentation, and they are
  // load-bearing for skills.ts — which imports them and IS checked, so a lie
  // in them surfaces over there — but nothing verifies them against the .mjs
  // code they sit in. Treat them as comments that happen to be
  // machine-readable, not as a guarantee.
  //
  // PHASE 2 added one file to that list: scripts/check-live-links.mjs, the
  // live-deployment link checker. Its decision-making — reference extraction,
  // internal/external classification, dist-path-to-URL mapping — is factored
  // out and unit-tested in tests/live-links.test.mjs precisely because the type
  // checker is not watching it.
  //
  // PHASE 3 added two more, and both are load-bearing:
  //
  //   src/loaders/site-pages.mjs   builds the five pages ABOUT the catalog,
  //                                including the verbatim README lifts
  //   scripts/prepare-assets.mjs   selects and copies the image assets that
  //                                SKILL.md bodies embed, before every build
  //
  // Neither is checked, and both are consumed by src/loaders/skills.ts, which
  // IS — so a shape mismatch at that boundary surfaces there. That is the only
  // type coverage they have. Their behaviour is covered by
  // tests/site-pages.test.mjs and tests/assets.test.mjs instead, for the same
  // reason the live-link checker's is.
  //
  // WHY IT IS NOT SIMPLY TURNED ON: `checkJs: true` surfaces errors that are
  // overwhelmingly missing annotations and implicit `any` under `strict` rather
  // than latent bugs. Fixing them is real work and out of scope. Logged as a
  // PHASE 5 CANDIDATE with a re-measured count so the phase can size it.
  //
  // RE-MEASURED IN FIX ROUND 2, AND THE OLD NUMBER WAS THE FINDING. This said
  // "204 errors (26 enumerate.mjs, 21 links.mjs, 14 markdown.mjs, 6
  // frontmatter.mjs, 5 sidebar.mjs, the rest in tests/ and .astro)" — a Phase 1
  // measurement quoted unchanged by a Phase 2 commit that edited the lines
  // directly above it to ADD a file to the unchecked list. Round 2 re-measured
  // it at 399.
  //
  // RE-MEASURED AGAIN IN PHASE 3, for the same reason and by the same method:
  // this edit adds two files to the list above, so the figure below it is
  // exactly the figure that would otherwise be inherited. Measured by flipping
  // `checkJs` to true, running `npx astro check`, and restoring the file —
  // `cmp` confirming the flip landed and the restore was byte-identical, and
  // `git status` producing the same output before and after.
  //
  // AND THEN RE-MEASURED ONCE MORE, because the first Phase 3 measurement was
  // taken mid-phase and four test files were added after it: the figure was
  // 501 across 22 files and is now 532 across 26. That is the same failure the
  // paragraph below warns about, caught inside a single phase. The number
  // quoted here is the one measured last, against the tree being committed:
  // 532 errors, 0 warnings, 8 hints, across 26 files.
  //
  //   scripts/check-live-links.mjs 62   tests/workflows 50
  //   tests/live-check-e2e 50   tests/enumeration 37   tests/_helpers 33
  //   tests/build-e2e 29   src/loaders/links.mjs 27
  //   src/loaders/enumerate.mjs 27   tests/pins 26
  //   src/loaders/site-pages.mjs 25   tests/chrome 23   tests/links 17
  //   tests/search-declaration 14   tests/link-rules 14
  //   src/loaders/markdown.mjs 14   tests/content 13   tests/live-links 12
  //   tests/assets 12   tests/no-fabrication 10   tests/fields 8
  //   tests/markdown 7   src/sidebar.mjs 6   src/loaders/frontmatter.mjs 6
  //   tests/site-pages 6   scripts/prepare-assets.mjs 3   tests/versions 1
  //
  // Phase 3 added THREE source files, and TWO of them are visible to this
  // census: src/loaders/site-pages.mjs 25 + scripts/prepare-assets.mjs 3 = 28
  // errors. The third, src/components/SiteIndex.astro, contributes 0 — not
  // because it is clean but because checkJs covers .mjs and .ts and this table
  // has no .astro row at all. The four test files Phase 3 added account for 27;
  // the remainder of the rise from Phase 2's 399 is in tests Phase 3 widened.
  // src/loaders/skills.ts stays at 0 because it is checked today.
  //
  // That sentence said "the two SOURCE files Phase 3 added" until the Phase 3
  // review caught it: three were added, and the count was over a population the
  // sentence did not name. The arithmetic was right and the word was wrong,
  // which is the failure this very comment goes on to warn about — one
  // paragraph below.
  //
  // The lesson is not the arithmetic, it is that a sizing figure sitting three
  // lines below an edit is exactly the figure nobody re-runs. Standard 2: a
  // number is re-measured at the moment it is quoted, not inherited.
  //
  // If you turn it on, do it as its own change with its own review. Do not
  // widen it as a side effect of something else, and do not restate the
  // coverage claim anywhere without changing this comment with it.
  // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  "extends": "astro/tsconfigs/strict",
  "include": [".astro/types.d.ts", "**/*"],
  "exclude": ["dist"],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true
  }
}
